       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/d7817a13e8d3b99719cbbbf7c9ee796b?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FA-6.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/d7817a13e8d3b99719cbbbf7c9ee796b?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FA-6.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/d7817a13e8d3b99719cbbbf7c9ee796b?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FA-6.png"
      },
      "displayName": "aliciac",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=5fca8aa42730d8007611e1e1",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>We ran into this as well. On startup, the fedora log shows:</p>\n\n<p>CREATE INDEX fcrepoRebuildStatus_rebuildDate ON fcrepoRebuildStatus (rebuildDate);<br/>\nERROR 2014-04-10 10:57:05.824 <span class=\"error\">&#91;pool-2-thread-1&#93;</span> (Server) Module (org.fcrepo.server.storage.DOManager) failed to initialize<br/>\norg.fcrepo.server.errors.ModuleInitializationException: Error while attempting to check for and create non-existing table(s): java.sql.SQLSyntaxErrorException: ORA-00902: invalid datatype</p>\n\n<p>It looks like bigint is also an invalid datatype in Oracle. </p>",
     "created": "10/Apr/14 5:58 PM",
     "id": "12588",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/11177/comment/12588",
     "updateAuthor": {
      "accountId": "5fca8aa42730d8007611e1e1",
